From: Darcy Phipps <dphipps@qnx.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Mar 2025 14:03:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 26/60] Get contrib/libarchive building with QNX8

QNX8 has the lz4.h header in a subdirectory of sysroot. Update
libarchive's build to deal with that.

3.0.24: libarchive 3.8.9 is built with CMake, so the configure.ac and source
changes no longer apply; the same intent (find the SDP's lz4.h under
usr/include/lz4/) is now a LZ4_INCLUDE_DIR setting.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific (from qnx-ports)

--- a/contrib/src/libarchive/rules.mak
+++ b/contrib/src/libarchive/rules.mak
@@ -20,6 +20,12 @@
 # bsdunzip doesn't build on macos, android and emscripten and it's disabled on Windows
 LIBARCHIVE_CONF +=-DENABLE_UNZIP=OFF
 
+ifdef HAVE_QNX
+# The QNX SDP keeps the LZ4 headers in usr/include/lz4/, where CMake's
+# find_path(lz4.h) does not look
+LIBARCHIVE_CONF += -DLZ4_INCLUDE_DIR=$(QNX_TARGET)/usr/include/lz4
+endif
+
 ifdef HAVE_MACOSX
 # these functions are detected as present but there are not until macOS 10.10
 # the minimum supported value is 10.7, in each case missing the functions falls
